Build the ALSA loopback driver

snd-aloop gives a pair of linked sound cards: what one program plays into
one end, another records from the other. It lets Kodi's decoded PCM go to a
separate process (a convolver for binaural headphone listening) instead of
straight to a device. Built as a module, so nothing changes until it is
loaded.

SND_DRIVERS only gates the generic drivers; the others it uncovers stay off.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/projects/Amlogic-ce/devices/Amlogic-no/linux/linux.aarch64.conf
+++ b/projects/Amlogic-ce/devices/Amlogic-no/linux/linux.aarch64.conf
@@ -4535,7 +4535,12 @@
 CONFIG_SND_CTL_FAST_LOOKUP=y
 # CONFIG_SND_DEBUG is not set
 # CONFIG_SND_SEQUENCER is not set
-# CONFIG_SND_DRIVERS is not set
+CONFIG_SND_DRIVERS=y
+# CONFIG_SND_DUMMY is not set
+CONFIG_SND_ALOOP=m
+# CONFIG_SND_MTPAV is not set
+# CONFIG_SND_SERIAL_U16550 is not set
+# CONFIG_SND_MPU401 is not set
 # CONFIG_SND_PCI is not set
 
 #
